                <pb facs="0232" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23530: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-27T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 28—5:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>81. Local press to-day published a telegram recently sent to President Carranza
                    by General Obregón asserting that the latter’s military <pb facs="0233" n="133"
                        xml:id="pg133"/> supporters for the Presidency are being persecuted while
                    those of Bonillas are given every protection and implying that this is being
                    done with the connivance of the Carranza administration, and a long telegram
                    from President Carranza in reply denying the assertion and severely criticising
                    General Obregón and his followers for their attitude in the campaign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
